{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.utsa.edu/people-excellence/careers/index.html": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers | People Excellence Search Bar Search News myUTSA Search Welcome to People Excellence Our Careers People Excellence About Mission Statement New Employees Before Your First Day New Hire Orientation First Month First Six Months New Employee Required Paperwork - Faculty/Students Professional Development Benefits Time and Leave Current Employees Benefits Time and Leave Compensation Performance Management Professional Development Wellness Workplace Injury Employee Self Service PeopleSource HR Business Partners Awards & Recognition Employee Records Planning for Retirement Dual Employment Manager Mid-Year Check In Checklist Employee Success Center Professional Development Performance Management Employee Wellness AllOne Health EAP Employee Benefits and Perks Employee Educational Benefit Awards and Recognition Occupational Health People Leaders Change Management eForms Employee Self Service Leadership Development Leadership Toolkit Professional Development Performance Management Recruitment Process SME Resources Time and Leave Talent Acquisition Temporary Staffing Support Retirees Retiree Benefits Return to Work for Retirees UT Retirement Programs COBRA Employee Records & Employment Verification W-2s and Paystubs Our Careers Faculty Positions Staff Positions Student Positions Resources PeopleSource Careers The University of Texas at San Antonio is a nationally recognized, top-tier public research university that unites the power of higher education, biomedical discovery and healthcare within one visionary institution. As the third-largest research university in Texas and a Carnegie R1-designated institution, UT San Antonio is a model of access and excellence — advancing knowledge, social mobility and public health across South Texas and beyond. Rooted in one of the country’s most dynamic and diverse metropolitan areas, UT San Antonio reflects the belief that great cities need great universities. We are the largest university in greater San Antonio with over 17,000 faculty and staff and more than 42,000 students. Explore Careers Faculty Positions Staff Positions Student Positions Working at UT San Antonio UT San Antonio’s dedication to excellence in higher education is reflected in its workforce. The university has been recognized by Forbes as one of America’s Best Employers for Company Culture in 2026. This recognition places the university nationally among the top organizations demonstrating excellence in workplace culture, including fairness, respect, mission connection and empowerment. Who We Are With more than 40,000 students, UT San Antonio is the largest university in the San Antonio metropolitan region, advancing knowledge through research and discovery, teaching and learning, community engagement and public service. The university serves as a center for intellectual and creative resources as well as a catalyst for socioeconomic development and the commercialization of intellectual property. Learn more about the great things happening at UT San Antonio. Leadership and Talent Development UT San Antonio is dedicated to the growth and development of all employees. A variety of learning opportunities are offered throughout the year in partnership with campus-wide subject matter experts that include topics related to specific job requirements, technical skills and leadership development. Benefits UT San Antonio offers competitive benefits package to all eligible employees and their dependents which includes medical, dental and vision options, leave, wellness support and more. Check out the many opportunities and services available to current employees. Roadrunner Community For a university that has only been around for a little over 50 years, UT San Antonio has rich traditions that convey our story of community and unite Roadrunners together. Our traditions help to tell our story and are interwoven into the fabric of the university. We are excited for you to join the UT San Antonio community and learn more about our history and Roadrunner traditions . UT San Antonio is proud to be a Ready to Work pledged employer. Ready to Work is an education and job placement program led by local employers to help thousands of people in San Antonio improve their quality of life and achieve professional success. The program offers participants an equitable, customized approach to acquire the skills needed to secure a higher-paying job by offering support services to overcome financial, mental and social challenges. Experience Our Campuses Birds Up! Learn more about UT San Antonio and the place our Roadrunners call home. Explore below to experience what it’s like to live, learn and work on our campuses. UT San Antonio: The College Tour UT San Antonio Virtual Tour Roadrunner Traditions People Excellence Phone: 210-458-4250 Fax: 210-458-4287 Email: hr@utsa.edu Address: One UTSA Circle NPB, Suite 451 San Antonio, Texas 78249 Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer As an equal employment opportunity and affirmative action employer, it is the policy of The University of Texas at San Antonio to promote and ensure equal employment opportunity for all individuals regardless of race, color, religion, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability or genetic information, and veteran status. The University is committed to the Affirmative Action Program in compliance with all government requirements to ensure nondiscrimination. Women, minorities, people with disabilities and veterans are encouraged to apply. UTSA campuses are accessible to persons with disabilities. For detailed information on workplace discrimination, view the \"Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal\" poster ( English , Spanish ). Complete list of posters and notices required by Federal and State law. For accommodation information for employees and applicants with disabilities, please review Disability Accommodation Guidelines and Procedures . One UTSA Circle, San Antonio, TX 78249 Information: 210-458-4011 @UTSA Facebook @UTSA Twitter @UTSA YouTube @UTSA LinkedIn @UTSA Instagram Careers Maps & Directions Directories University Organization © 2025 The University of Texas at San Antonio Emergency Response Guide Policies Web Accessibility Required Links UT System"
    },
    "https://www.utsa.edu/people-excellence/careers/faculty-positions.html": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions",
      "description": "Faculty Positions | People Excellence Search Bar Search News myUTSA Search Welcome to People Excellence Our Careers Faculty Positions People Excellence About Mission Statement New Employees Before Your First Day New Hire Orientation First Month First Six Months New Employee Required Paperwork - Faculty/Students Professional Development Benefits Time and Leave Current Employees Benefits Time and Leave Compensation Performance Management Professional Development Wellness Workplace Injury Employee Self Service PeopleSource HR Business Partners Awards & Recognition Employee Records Planning for Retirement Dual Employment Manager Mid-Year Check In Checklist Employee Success Center Professional Development Performance Management Employee Wellness AllOne Health EAP Employee Benefits and Perks Employee Educational Benefit Awards and Recognition Occupational Health People Leaders Change Management eForms Employee Self Service Leadership Development Leadership Toolkit Professional Development Performance Management Recruitment Process SME Resources Time and Leave Talent Acquisition Temporary Staffing Support Retirees Retiree Benefits Return to Work for Retirees UT Retirement Programs COBRA Employee Records & Employment Verification W-2s and Paystubs Our Careers Faculty Positions Staff Positions Student Positions Resources PeopleSource Faculty Positions Thank you for your interest in a career with UT San Antonio. As a Tier One research university, we provide excellence in higher education and serve as a catalyst for socioeconomic development. We are dedicated to identifying, recruiting and retaining highly qualified, talented faculty. We're proud to have been named a top employer in Texas by Forbes in 2022 and 2023. View open faculty positions at the links below. You must complete an application to be considered for a position at the university. External Applicants Search for Current Openings and Apply as an External Applicant Help New Users To search for positions , select from the menu options located on the left navigation menu. To apply for a job, register for a new user account by clicking the New User link located on the top navigation bar. Returning Users Click the Sign In link located on the top navigation bar, enter your username and password. This enables you to: Edit your existing account settings. Apply for new jobs. Review the status of positions you have applied to. Email postings to a friend. If you're having trouble applying or have questions, see the Troubleshooting Guide and FAQ . Internal Applicants Search for Current Openings and Apply as an Internal Applicant Help In Employee Self-Service , click on the Staff Careers tile. Search for current openings by keyword, location, department or job family. Assistance is available upon request. Office hours are Monday through Friday, 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. For additional information, contact People Excellence at (210) 458-4250. Applicants can obtain information concerning accommodation in the application process by emailing the ADA Coordinator . Final candidates for employment must successfully pass a Criminal Background Check (CBC) as all positions at UTSA are security sensitive. If you're having trouble applying or have questions, see the Troubleshooting Guide and FAQ . Total Rewards Package We offer a comprehensive benefits package including: Medical, Dental & Vision Benefits Leave Types Wellness Programs Retirement Programs Professional Development Awards & Recognition Programs Employee Assistance Program Employee Educational Benefit Employee Discount Program Applicant Resources & Information Visit the Applicant Resources and Information page to access important resources, including the applicant troubleshooting guide, disability accommodation details, the university's promotion/transfer policy for probationary employees, LCA postings for H1-B purposes, and information for former foster youth, non-citizen and veteran applicants. Annual Campus Security Report Each year The University of Texas at San Antonio publishes the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act. This report contains crime statistics and on-campus housing fire statistics for the three most recent calendar years. The report includes institutional policies concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, crime reporting, sexual assault, and other crime-related issues. You can obtain a copy of this report by contacting the Clery Compliance Coordinator at 210-458-4153 or by accessing the Clery Compliance website . People Excellence Phone: 210-458-4250 Fax: 210-458-4287 Email: hr@utsa.edu Address: One UTSA Circle NPB, Suite 451 San Antonio, Texas 78249 Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer As an equal employment opportunity and affirmative action employer, it is the policy of The University of Texas at San Antonio to promote and ensure equal employment opportunity for all individuals regardless of race, color, religion, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability or genetic information, and veteran status. The University is committed to the Affirmative Action Program in compliance with all government requirements to ensure nondiscrimination. Women, minorities, people with disabilities and veterans are encouraged to apply. UTSA campuses are accessible to persons with disabilities. For detailed information on workplace discrimination, view the \"Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal\" poster ( English , Spanish ). Complete list of posters and notices required by Federal and State law. For accommodation information for employees and applicants with disabilities, please review: UTSA Disability Accommodation Guidelines and Procedures . One UTSA Circle, San Antonio, TX 78249 Information: 210-458-4011 @UTSA Facebook @UTSA Twitter @UTSA YouTube @UTSA LinkedIn @UTSA Instagram Careers Maps & Directions Directories University Organization © 2025 The University of Texas at San Antonio Emergency Response Guide Policies Web Accessibility Required Links UT System"
    },
