    "https://www.utsa.edu/people-excellence/careers/student-positions.html": {
      "title": "Student Positions",
      "description": "Student Positions | People Excellence Search Bar Search News myUTSA Search Welcome to People Excellence Our Careers Student Positions People Excellence About Mission Statement New Employees Before Your First Day New Hire Orientation First Month First Six Months New Employee Required Paperwork - Faculty/Students Professional Development Benefits Time and Leave Current Employees Benefits Time and Leave Compensation Performance Management Professional Development Wellness Workplace Injury Employee Self Service PeopleSource HR Business Partners Awards & Recognition Employee Records Planning for Retirement Dual Employment Manager Mid-Year Check In Checklist Employee Success Center Professional Development Performance Management Employee Wellness AllOne Health EAP Employee Benefits and Perks Employee Educational Benefit Awards and Recognition Occupational Health People Leaders Change Management eForms Employee Self Service Leadership Development Leadership Toolkit Professional Development Performance Management Recruitment Process SME Resources Time and Leave Talent Acquisition Temporary Staffing Support Retirees Retiree Benefits Return to Work for Retirees UT Retirement Programs COBRA Employee Records & Employment Verification W-2s and Paystubs Our Careers Faculty Positions Staff Positions Student Positions Resources PeopleSource About New Employees Current Employees Employee Success Center People Leaders Retirees & Former Employees Our Careers Faculty Positions Staff Positions Student Positions Resources & Tools Student Positions At The University of Texas at San Antonio, students make up an important and valued part of the workforce. Through these opportunities, students are provided with support in pursuit of their academic goals and opportunities for academic or administrative job experience. The Career Center and Student Success provide numerous opportunities for students to build career-related skills and connect with employers through career events. Log into Handshake to search for on-campus and off-campus positions. Undergraduate Students There are more than 600 students in positions throughout various departments on campus. Each position is focused on developing the individual’s marketable leadership skills and career preparation. The student workforce is central to the operations of campus buildings and vital to programs and services. Undergraduate and graduate students are eligible for student employment positions. Visit Student Affairs for more information on student employment and internships. Graduate Students There are several types of assistantships available to graduate students. Specific job descriptions are available from the hiring department. Assignments cannot exceed 19 hours per week and there are minimum enrollment requirements for each position. Learn more about graduate student benefits , or visit The Graduate School for more information on the types of positions, funding opportunities, and eligibility requirements, etc. Annual Campus Security Report Each year The University of Texas at San Antonio publishes the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act. This report contains crime statistics and on-campus housing fire statistics for the three most recent calendar years. The report includes institutional policies concerning campus security, alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, crime reporting, sexual assault, and other crime-related issues. You can obtain a copy of this report by contacting the Clery Compliance Coordinator at 210-458-4153 or by accessing the Clery Compliance website . People Excellence Phone: 210-458-4250 Fax: 210-458-4287 Email: hr@utsa.edu Address: One UTSA Circle NPB, Suite 451 San Antonio, Texas 78249 Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer As an equal employment opportunity and affirmative action employer, it is the policy of The University of Texas at San Antonio to promote and ensure equal employment opportunity for all individuals regardless of race, color, religion, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability or genetic information, and veteran status. The University is committed to the Affirmative Action Program in compliance with all government requirements to ensure nondiscrimination. Women, minorities, people with disabilities and veterans are encouraged to apply. UTSA campuses are accessible to persons with disabilities. For detailed information on workplace discrimination, view the \"Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal\" poster ( English , Spanish ). Complete list of posters and notices required by Federal and State law. For accommodation information for employees and applicants with disabilities, please review: UTSA Disability Accommodation Guidelines and Procedures . One UTSA Circle, San Antonio, TX 78249 Information: 210-458-4011 @UTSA Facebook @UTSA Twitter @UTSA YouTube @UTSA LinkedIn @UTSA Instagram Careers Maps & Directions Directories University Organization © 2025 The University of Texas at San Antonio Emergency Response Guide Policies Web Accessibility Required Links UT System"
    }
